<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-RIO DE JANEIRO CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-RIO DE JANEIRO CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Rio de</p>
<p>Janeiro championship matches played Wednesday.</p>
<p> Botafogo		   1   Flamengo			0</p>
<p> Madureira		  2   Fluminense		    1</p>
<p> Barreira		   1   Olaria			  0</p>
<p> Americano		  1   Volta Redonda		 0</p>
<p> Bangu			1   America/Rio de Janeiro    1</p>
<p>     Standings	     P  W  D  L  F    A  Pts</p>
<p>  1. Botafogo	     11 11  0  0  29   8  33</p>
<p>  2. Vasco da Gama	11  8  1  2  21  11  25</p>
<p>  3. Flamengo	     11  7  3  1  31   8  24</p>
<p>  4. Madureira	    11  6  0  5  14  16  18</p>
<p>  5. Bangu		  11  4  4  3  19  19  16</p>
<p>  6. Fluminense	   11  4  3  4  13  13  15</p>
<p>  7. Americano	    11  4  1  6  10  13  13</p>
<p>  8. Volta Redonda	11  3  3  5  13  16  12</p>
<p>  9. America		11  1  6  4   9  13   9</p>
<p> 10. Itaperuna	    11  2  1  8   9  21   7</p>
<p> 11. Barreira	     11  2  1  8   8  28   7</p>
<p> 12. Olaria		 11  1  3  7  11  21   6</p>
<p>Note: top two teams play off to decide the first stage</p>
<p>winners.</p>
<p>The winners of the first, second and third stages each</p>
<p>qualify for the final play-off stage. Only the top eight teams</p>
<p>in the first stage continue into the second stage and only the</p>
<p>top six in the second stage carry on into the third.</p>
<p>There is no play off in the second and third stages. The</p>
<p>team that finishes at the top after the teams have played each</p>
<p>other once wins the stage.</p>
</text>
